course: dictionary
lesson: 15330
title: Snobby: looking down on others
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Snobby means acting like a snob. A snob thinks they are better than other people because of their money, their class or their taste, and they look down on everyone else. Context gives clues: «Mia would only sit at the table nearest the window, and she sniffed at the cheap sandwiches.» Sniffing at things and wanting only the best shows she thinks she is above others, so snobby fits.
explain: Snobby can also describe a place or a thing. «The snobby restaurant had a doorman and tiny plates of food, and nobody in our class could afford it.» Here it means posh and unfriendly to ordinary people. The clues are the doorman, the tiny plates and the high price.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Does «Mia was thinking she was better than the sandwiches» make sense? Look at what the person does and says, and you will find the meaning. Snobbish means the same thing and is the more standard word, but snobby is a little more informal.
fact: Snobby means acting like a snob: thinking you are better than others and looking down on them.
fact: Snobby can describe a person's attitude, such as «a snobby attitude».
fact: Snobby can also describe a place or thing that seems posh and unfriendly to ordinary people, such as «a snobby school».
fact: Snobbish means the same as snobby and is the more standard word.
exercise: «Ben would only talk to people with big houses, and he rolled his eyes at everyone else.» What does snobby mean here? | Very sleepy | Afraid of big houses | Kind and generous to everyone | *Thinking he is better than other people
exercise: «The snobby café only served tiny cakes on silver plates.» What does snobby describe? | *A café that seems posh and unfriendly to ordinary people | A café that is loud and messy | A café that is closed on Sundays | A café that sells only hot dogs
exercise: Which word is the more standard word for snobby? | sleepy | snowy | *snobbish | silly
test: «Nadia was snobby about her new school and said the other children were beneath her.» What does snobby suggest? | *Looking down on others | Feeling very cold | Playing too loudly
test: Which sentence describes a place as posh and unfriendly? | We played football in the garden | Sam shared his crisps with everyone | *The snobby hotel made us feel we did not belong | The park was full of rain
exam: Which word could replace snobby in «Lily was snobby about Sam's old bike» without changing the meaning? | Shy | *Stuck-up | Friendly | Modest
